<title>USA: U.S. reviewing Dutch swine fever outbreak.</title>
<headline>U.S. reviewing Dutch swine fever outbreak.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department's Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service (APHIS) is looking into a recent outbreak of swine fever in the Netherlands and it is too early to say if any restrictions might be set on imports, an APHIS spokeswoman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're in the reviewing and information gathering stages,&quot; said the spokeswoman, who asked not to be identified.</p>
<p>The U.S. imports swine and swine products from the Netherlands, which has a hog cholera-free status.</p>
<p>The Dutch goverment said Tuesday it had discovered an outbreak of swine fever in the south of the country and as a precaution had closed off the one farm involved and two nearby slaughterhouses.</p>
